## Spec B8 (docs/specs/stdlib/executor.spec.md): block_on drives
## a sub-phase-2B chained-await future to completion across multiple
## suspension points.
##
## The outer future has two `.await`s, so its state machine has 3
## states (state 0 polls inner_a, state 1 polls inner_b, terminal
## fold inside state 1). Per spec B5 of the lowering, transitions
## return Pending between states (no eager fall-through), so the
## block_on poll loop polls outer 3 times — yielding between each —
## before reaching Ready(30).
##
## Pinned behaviours:
##   B8 — block_on correctly drives a multi-state future past every
##        Poll.Pending the lowering emits, returning Ready(30) only
##        when the final state's continuation produces it.

async def inner_a() -> Int
  10
end

async def inner_b() -> Int
  20
end

async def outer() -> Int
  let a = inner_a().await
  let b = inner_b().await
  a + b
end

def main
  let result = block_on(outer())
  puts "#{result}"
end
